# This was a 119-line ALLOWLIST until 2026-07-30, and it had to be: the repo
# root was literally ~/.config — a 9.6 GB directory full of browser profiles,
# Electron app data, game launchers and real credentials. Ignoring everything
# with `/*` and un-ignoring 38 known-good paths was the only safe rule, and the
# cost was that any new directory stayed invisible to git until someone
# remembered to add a `!/name/` line for it.
#
# The restructure moved the dotfiles under `dotfiles/` and put the flake at the
# repo root, so this is an ordinary project root now — and an ordinary
# denylist. Add a new config directory by just adding it.

# --- Generated at runtime, not configuration --------------------------------
# The mode scripts write this; the rest of home/mango/ is tracked input.
/dotfiles/mango/config.conf

# `/dotfiles/mango/walker/config.toml` was the second rule here until
# 2026-08-14. Each autostart.conf symlinked its mode's walker config over that
# path, so it was a generated symlink AND tracked in git — two owners on one
# path, and activation failed with "would be clobbered" only after a mode
# switch had created it, long after the change that caused it. walker is gone
# (docs/adr/0021) and rofi has one config for every mode, so the whole class
# goes with it. Left as a note because the shape recurs: anything an
# autostart.conf writes must not also be tracked.

# Runtime state moved to ~/.local/state/mango on 2026-07-30. Kept as a rule so
# an old checkout or a stray script cannot quietly reintroduce state into the
# config tree — state living there is what forced ~/.config/mango to stay
# writable, and it left `pia-auth` (PIA credentials, mode 600) sitting inside
# the repo relying on this file to stay out of history.
/dotfiles/mango/state/

# dotfiles/kitty/ and dotfiles/foot/ are gone entirely as of 2026-08-01 — both
# terminals are generated by `programs.kitty` / `programs.foot` in
# modules/home/programs.nix, so there is no directory left for a mode script to
# write a theme into. The active-theme.* rules that stood here are dropped with
# them; that indirection was already removed on 2026-07-30 (both modes pointed
# it at the same gruvbox files, so it selected nothing).

# --- User data, not config --------------------------------------------------
# The wallpaper MOVED OUT of the config tree on 2026-07-30, to
# ~/.local/share/mango/wallpaper.png — the same reasoning that moved runtime
# state to ~/.local/state/mango. It was the last thing blocking a store-based
# dotfiles/mango/: flakes copy only git-tracked files, so an ignored 4.6 MB PNG
# would simply not exist under a read-only ~/.config/mango.
# The rule is kept so a stray script cannot quietly reintroduce it.
/dotfiles/mango/wallpaper/

# --- Credentials ------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT linked by dotfiles.nix and restored by hand. Listed so an
# accidental `git add -A` cannot pull them in.
/dotfiles/gh/
/dotfiles/glab-cli/
/dotfiles/gpu-screen-recorder/
/dotfiles/opencode/
/dotfiles/rclone/
/dotfiles/rbw/
/dotfiles/tea/

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# secrets/*.yaml is sops-ENCRYPTED and deliberately tracked — that is the whole
# point. What must never land here is an age private key. The real one lives at
# /var/lib/sops-nix/key.txt, outside the repo; these rules only catch a stray
# copy. checks/static.sh asserts every secrets/*.yaml carries sops metadata.
*.age
key.txt
keys.txt

# --- Caches, history, scratch ----------------------------------------------
/dotfiles/zsh/.zsh_history
/dotfiles/zsh/.zcompdump*
/dotfiles/zsh/.zcompcache/
/dotfiles/zsh/.zsh_tmp_git_*
**/*.log
**/*.tmp
**/cache/
**/Cache/

# --- Build output and editor noise ------------------------------------------
result
result-*
.direnv/
*.hm-bak
*.arch-bak
*.swp
*~

# dotfiles/ncspot/ is gone as of 2026-08-01 — `programs.ncspot` generates
# config.toml, and userstate.cbor was only ever written to ~/.config/ncspot/,
# never here. The copy in the repo was residue from before docs/adr/0003 and
# had been untracked-but-present ever since; it is deleted rather than ignored.
